":"f4b90280-caa4-4a3c-bc2e-c3342789f24d"}],"links":[["facility","facility"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"pound"},{"word":"shelter"}],"glosses":["A facility at which dogs are reared or boarded."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"32e2160f-8699-42cd-8c20-118cc81fd622"},{"examples":[{"text":"A little herd of England's timorous deer, / Mazed with a yelping kennel of French curs!","ref":"1591, William Shakespeare, Henry VI, Part 1, act 4, scene 2:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[65,71]],"id":"9664a9c9-2d99-4eb4-923d-5fe4733e25a5"},{"text":"A world of mere Patent-Digesters will soon have nothing to digest: such world ends, and by Law of Nature must end, in ‘over-population;’ in howling universal famine, ‘impossibility,’ and suicidal madness, as of endless dog-kennels run rabid.","ref":"1843, Thomas Carlyle, “IX: Working Aristocracy”, in Past and Present, book 3:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[223,230]],"id":"9bfeefd5-b945-4755-819e-a98d7dd2759f"}],"categories":["British English","English collective nouns","English terms with quotations"],"synonyms":[{"word":"pack"}],"raw_glosses":["(UK, collective) The dogs kept at such a facility; a pack of hounds."],"glosses":["The dogs kept at such a facility; a pack of hounds."],"tags":["UK","collective"],"id":"32bd181b-ec07-4644-a022-7ebaefb69276"},{"links":[["fox","fox"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"burrow"},{"word":"den"}],"glosses":["The hole of a fox or other animal."],"id":"b338bf50-7e1b-4032-85ea-96e06dc120c0"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"Kenyan":{"id":"f2680fad-3abc-419d-97e9-629b458a8c28","word":"Kenyan","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Of, from, or pertaining to Kenya or the Kenyan people","word":"queniano"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"glosses":["Of, from, or pertaining to Kenya or the Kenyan people."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"c69bcde0-4aaf-415e-9a7a-d2c991f8c6d9"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"Kentucky":{"id":"b42efc52-88b4-4748-a1fd-6d9ec222b604","word":"Kentucky","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"US state","tags":["masculine"],"word":"Kentucky"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"On the invitation list: Govs. Andy Beshear of Kentucky, Tim Walz of Minnesota, J.B. Pritzker of Illinois, Gretchen Whitmer of Michigan, Tony Evers of Wisconsin, Josh Shapiro of Pennsylvania, Roy Cooper of North Carolina, Wes Moore of Maryland and Michelle Lujan Grisham of New Mexico.","ref":"2024 February 7, Edward-Isaac Dovere, “Harris set to host Democratic governors this weekend to discuss 2024 campaign”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[46,54]],"id":"8a74a10a-c7c4-4b74-b0cf-0313147e3bb4"},{"text":"The chicken chain’s parent company, Yum Brands, announced Tuesday that KFC’s corporate headquarters is leaving Kentucky for Texas, joining sister brand Pizza Hut’s offices in the Dallas suburb of Plano.","ref":"2025 February 19, Jordan Valinsky, “KFC is leaving Kentucky”, in CNN Business:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[111,119]],"id":"2694a715-5cd4-48e1-ba49-da113ffb78a1"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Kentucky, USA","en:Places in the United States","en:States of the United States"],"links":[["state","state"],["United States","United States#English"],["Frankfort","Frankfort#English"],["Louisville","Louisville#English"],["Commonwealth","Commonwealth"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"Bluegrass State"},{"word":"Corn-cracker State"},{"word":"Dark and Bloody Ground State"},{"word":"Hemp State"},{"word":"Kaintuck"},{"word":"Tobacco State"}],"glosses":["A state of the United States. Capital: Frankfort. Largest city: Louisville. Formally known as the Commonwealth of Kentucky, one of four such states known as Commonwealths."],"id":"42563166-4a51-497d-9449-1d8e65544cba"},{"categories":["en:Places in Australia","en:Places in New South Wales, Australia","en:Villages in Australia","en:Villages in New South Wales, Australia"],"links":[["village","v