tates","en:Unincorporated communities in Texas, USA"],"links":[["United States","United States#English"],["unincorporated community","unincorporated community"],["Culberson County","Culberson County#English"],["Texas","Texas#English"]],"glosses":["A number of places in the United States:","An unincorporated community in Culberson County, Texas."],"id":"dcff7725-abd7-4108-8fc1-03f60c4cb74f"},{"categories":["en:Cities in Washington, USA","en:Cities in the United States","en:Places in Seattle","en:Places in Washington, USA","en:Places in the United States","en:Suburbs of Seattle"],"links":[["United States","United States#English"],["city","city"],["King County","King County#English"],["Washington","Washington#English"],["United States","United States#English"],["suburb","suburb"],["Seattle","Seattle#English"]],"glosses":["A number of places in the United States:","A city in King County, Washington, United States; a suburb of Seattle."],"id":"3e960a9d-e0a2-44c3-b019-3980e1c2dee1"},{"categories":["en:Neighborhoods of Washington, D.C.","en:Places in Washington, D.C.","en:Places in the United States"],"links":[["United States","United States#English"],["neighborhood","neighborhood"],["Washington, D.C.","Washington, D.C.#English"]],"glosses":["A number of places in the United States:","A neighborhood in northwest Washington, D.C.."],"id":"80a4e884-3d12-42d3-82a7-84623eb397ee"},{"categories":["en:Places in West Virginia, USA","en:Places in the United States","en:Unincorporated communities in West Virginia, USA"],"links":[["United States","United States#English"],["unincorporated community","unincorporated community"],["Marshall County","Marshall County#English"],["West Virginia","West Virginia#English"]],"glosses":["A number of places in the United States:","An unincorporated community in Marshall County, West Virginia."],"id":"686c2375-1ca9-4c85-b1e0-d31a20fe46b1"},{"categories":["English surnames","English surnames from Old English"],"links":[["surname","surname"]],"glosses":["A surname from Old English derived from the place name."],"id":"951aacf7-ee67-455b-a9d8-ab508610342f"},{"examples":[{"text":"Kent Syler, a professor of political science at Middle Tennessee State University, told Newsweek in an interview Tuesday evening that the \"aggressive\" gerrymandering will make it \"very, very difficult\" for Democrats to hold the seat in the 2022 midterms.","ref":"2022 January 25, Andrew Stanton, “Jim Cooper Calls Out ‘Gerrymandering’ of Tennessee District, Will Not Seek Re-Election”, in Newsweek:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[0,4]],"id":"5d30f141-9994-4801-8e2c-c823de536010"}],"categories":["English given names","English male given names","English male given names from surnames","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["given name","given name"]],"glosses":["A male given name transferred from the surname, of mostly American usage."],"id":"d7174a4d-e09d-4196-aece-d58af00e5360"},{"links":[["royal","royal#English"],["dukedom","dukedom#English"]],"glosses":["A royal dukedom."],"id":"6ee528c4-acd2-4d56-a06c-c5afd0747904"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"Kenneth":{"id":"1409f062-4b1e-4f05-ae83-cd221f39dba6","word":"Kenneth","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"male given name","word":"Kenneth"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Know, however, that among the soldiers of the Cross I am called Kenneth - Kenneth of the Couching Leopard; at home I have other titles, but they would sound harsh in an Eastern ear.","ref":"1825, Sir Walter Scott, chapter III, in The Talisman:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[64,71],[74,81]],"id":"1203d416-af82-400a-901b-70930f562d88"},{"text":"\"The other one, his name was Kenneth, was born in February nineteen twenty-one.\"\n\"All these Kens,\" she said.","ref":"1998 Barbara Vine ( Ruth Rendell ): The Chimney Sweeper's Boy. →ISBN page 166","roman":"\"As you say. It must have been the sexy name. These days Kens are all Chinese cooks. - - -","